; autolanding info
; aerodrome/poi = type (heli,rwy,goaround), direction (n, w, s, e; x for don't care), altitude, runway length in meters (ignored for heli)
; IF TYPE IS goaround, the format changes:
; random id = "goaround", starting point X, starting point Y, ending point X, ending point Y, altitude
; an FMS should be able to circle into the goaround route, fly straight, circle back to runway line, realign, and try landing again.
; Minecraft coord convention:
; North: Z-
; East: X+
; South: Z+
; West: X-
; Altitude: Y axis
TMU=heli,n,69,0
AGS=heli,n,73,0
BZR=heli,w,69,0
ZTP=heli,s,70,0
KST=heli,w,71,0
FRO=heli,s,73,0
WAU=heli,s,120,0
ARN=heli,s,70,0
RNF=heli,n,70,0
WCL=heli,e,226,0
FRT=heli,w,93,0
TWN=heli,e,73,0
OLV=heli,w,73,0
TMV=rwy,s,69,295
TMA=rwy,n,69,295
TMA_GA=goaround,780,262,780,1229,105
TMV_GA=goaround,780,1229,780,262,105
